\subsection{Simulation results}
\Cref{table1} shows that UP-VLA attains an average length of 4.08 on ABC$\rightarrow$D, against 3.06 for GR-1 (about 33\% higher), 3.35 for 3D Diffuser Actor, 2.47 for RoboFlamingo and 1.44 for UP-VLA-RT-2. The gap grows with chain length: success on the fifth task is 0.699, versus 0.401 for GR-1. The GR-1-like UP-VLA-phi-w/o-mmu reaches 3.13, so adding MMU and joint conditioning on the same backbone raises the average by about 0.95. 3D Diffuser Actor is the only method with a higher first-task success than UP-VLA (0.938 vs.\ 0.928). On ABCD$\rightarrow$D (\cref{table2}) UP-VLA obtains 4.42, compared with 4.21 for GR-1 and 4.09 for RoboFlamingo; the margin is smaller since all scenes are seen in training.

